# Milestone: M3
# Covers: loop body with break/continue is desugared only once; '&' inside a
#         while loop fires both echo calls before breaking.
# blocked: needs a `## host:` body.  The host driver has existed since
# the core re-foundation (tests/integration/chk_host_driver.c) -- what is
# missing is this fixture, rewritten to drive its own clock and its own
# urbi_step calls.  That is per-fixture authoring work, scheduled with the
# rest of the corpus in Phase 5.  The annotation it replaced said the
# driver did not exist, which stopped being true at Task 12.
# matrix-row: separator-and
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture uses '&' inside while/for loop bodies to verify that the AST is
#   not incorrectly re-desugared on each iteration.  '&' requires the M5 chk
#   driver (realm-managed scheduler path).  The cooperative scheduler's loop
#   body handling with break/continue is separately verified at the unit-test
#   level in M3.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with urbi_step chk driver):
# # while(true) { echo(1) & echo(1); break };
# # [00000001] *** 1
# # [00000002] *** 1
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/multiple-visit.chk)
